.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt BRCM-FBSD-CONFIGURATOR 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm brcm-fbsd-configurator
.Nd configure Wi-Fi for the if_bcm4313 driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm menu | status | scan | diagnose | version
.Nm
.Cm connect
.Op Fl boot | ping | recreate | open
.Op Fl password-file Ar file | ask-password
.Op Fl timeout Ar seconds
.Ar ssid
.Nm
.Cm wpa
.Op Fl boot | ping | recreate
.Op Fl timeout Ar seconds
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates or reuses a net80211 VAP over an
.Xr if_bcm4313 4
parent device, scans for networks, joins open or WPA/WPA2 networks, requests an IPv4 address with DHCP, and optionally persists the configuration for boot.
.Pp
The driver must already be installed and loaded.
Protected networks use
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
with the FreeBSD
.Fl Dbsd
backend.
Passwords are read from a hidden prompt, a file, or standard input; they are not accepted as positional arguments.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width status
.It Cm menu
Run the interactive menu.
.Cm scan
Prepare the VAP and print normalized scan results.
.It Cm connect
Join the specified SSID.
Use
.Cm open
for an open network, or provide a password with
.Cm password-file
or
.Cm ask-password .
.It Cm wpa
Join using an existing
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5
file.
.It Cm status
Print driver, device, interface, address, route, and counter status.
.It Cm diagnose
Print a labeled diagnostic report.
.It Cm version
Print the program version.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--password-file file"
.It Fl boot
Persist the WPA configuration and required
.Xr rc.conf 5
keys.
.It Fl ping
Ping 8.8.8.8 after DHCP.
.It Fl recreate
Destroy and recreate an existing VAP when necessary.
.It Fl open
Join an open network.
.It Fl password-file Ar file
Read the passphrase from
.Ar file .
Use
.Fl
for standard input.
.It Fl ask-password
Prompt with terminal echo disabled.
.It Fl timeout Ar seconds
Set the association timeout.
.It Fl force
Replace an existing generated WPA configuration in boot mode.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BRCM_WPA_CONF"
.It Ev WLANIF
VAP interface name; defaults to
.Li wlan0 .
.It Ev WLDEV
Parent device; defaults to the first
.Li bcm4313*
entry in
.Li net.wlan.devices .
.It Ev TIMEOUT
Association timeout in seconds; defaults to 30.
.It Ev BRCM_RC_CONF
Boot configuration file; defaults to
.Pa /etc/rc.conf .
.It Ev BRCM_WPA_CONF
Persistent WPA configuration; defaults to
.Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf .
.It Ev BRCM_CTRL_DIR
Supplicant control directory; defaults to
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant .
.It Ev NO_TUI
Disable dialog and interactive menus when set.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
Generated WPA configurations are written with mode 0600.
The plaintext PSK comment emitted by
.Xr wpa_passphrase 8
is removed.
Existing interfaces are not destroyed unless
.Fl recreate
is supplied, and existing persistent WPA files are not overwritten without
.Fl force .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Scan and join from the menu:
.Pp
.Dl sudo brcm-fbsd-configurator
.Pp
Join a protected network and enable boot reconnect:
.Pp
.Dl sudo brcm-fbsd-configurator connect --ask-password --boot MyNetwork
.Pp
Join an open network:
.Pp
.Dl sudo brcm-fbsd-configurator connect --open MyOpenNetwork
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
.Xr wpa_passphrase 8 ,
.Xr dhclient 8 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
